{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789496211,"nonce":"ImoR459qBgtqsm0NYItE+se0LmU=","title":"Arbitrary-precision int for pidigits","message":"pidigits computes digits of pi with integers of thousands of bits; on zypy's 64-bit int it finishes in 10 ms with a wrong answer it does not print, so the harness marks it unmet rather than reporting a time. A bigint is an opt-in stdlib type by design (47a9c86); this kernel needs it to be the type `int` promotes to on overflow, or a way to declare the kernel's ints as such without editing it. Gap list 89aaf85.","files":null}]}